        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Flood Advisory issued November 13 at 4:14AM PST until November 13 at 6:15AM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Riverside County in southern California...\nSoutheastern Orange County in southwestern California...\nWestern San Diego County in southwestern California...\n\n* WHEN...Until 615 AM PST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nWater over roadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 414 AM PST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. This  will cause urban and small stream flooding.\nBetween 0.25 and 0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up...",
        "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
        "response": "Avoid",
